  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Communication, Coordination, and Improving Local Capacities and Partnerships in Libya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The Libya International Non Governmental Organization (INGO) Forum (LIF) is an independent network of 30 INGOs operating in Libya, with headquarters spread across over 8 different countries and who deliver a broad range of humanitarian, development, and peacebuilding programs in Libya. Established in 2016, LIF is led by a Country Director supported by the LIF Secretariat, who together plays a crucial role in amplifying the voices of INGOs in Libya, with a primary aim of fostering collaborative efforts in tackling significant challenges of mutual concern, leading to coherent and efficient program implementation. The LIF and INGO members are guided by and committed to the fundamental humanitarian principles of humanity, impartiality, neutrality, and independence. The guiding principles serves as beacons throughout every stage of the program cycle, ensuring that aid and assistance is delivered with integrity and a commitment to serving the needs of affected communities in Libya. LIF is currently hosted by the IRC, see &lt;em&gt;annex 1&lt;/em&gt;, Hosting Agreement, for more details.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
